01:49:08.590 --> 01:49:10.270
that are yet to be published.

01:49:10.270 --> 01:49:12.470
And I also was excited to do this episode

01:49:12.470 --> 01:49:14.440
because I think many of us have heard

01:49:14.440 --> 01:49:15.670
about the gut microbiome.

01:49:15.670 --> 01:49:17.900
We hear about these bacteria
that live in our gut.

01:49:17.900 --> 01:49:19.610
We hear about the gut-brain axis

01:49:19.610 --> 01:49:22.770
or that 90% or more of
the serotonin that we make

01:49:22.770 --> 01:49:23.810
is made in our gut.

01:49:23.810 --> 01:49:26.490
We hear about the gut as a
second brain and so forth.

01:49:26.490 --> 01:49:28.890
But I think for many people,

01:49:28.890 --> 01:49:30.710
they don't really have a clear picture

01:49:30.710 --> 01:49:32.430
of what the gut microbiome is

01:49:32.430 --> 01:49:35.580
and the pathways and mechanisms
by which it can signal

01:49:35.580 --> 01:49:37.920
to the brain and to the
other parts of the body.

01:49:37.920 --> 01:49:40.610
So I hope that today's
information at least improved

01:49:40.610 --> 01:49:42.640
